-- §6.3 quiescence drain, INFERRED-scheme half of #3031.
--
-- `top`'s scheme is INFERRED, and it quantifies the receiver `Sh a` carries.  At
-- graph quiescence the drain replays that goal with `a` still an unbound `TVar`.
-- `routeUndeterminedTop`'s ambiguous arm must ask whether some scheme QUANTIFIES
-- the variable (the `deferrableVarIds`/`goalsClosed` test) and defer such a goal to
-- its caller; reporting it as ambiguous, at a stale location, was #3031.
--
-- SPEC ANSWER, hand-derived before running anything: `main` calls `top` at
-- `Bool`, `h` forwards to `needsSh`, `impl Sh Bool` is the unique match, so the
-- program prints 22 on every engine and `check` accepts.  `11`/`22` sit at a
-- declared `Int` return position, fully grounded, so they are not the
-- undefaulted-`Num` class #2646 owes — the ambiguity is manufactured by the drain.
--
-- WHAT THIS ROW PINS: `check` must NOT report `T-AMBIGUOUS-INSTANCE`.  The drain's
-- own verdict is read in-process by `compiler/types/typecheck_test.mdk`.
interface Sh a where
  shv : a -> Int

impl Sh Int where
  shv _ = 11

impl Sh Bool where
  shv _ = 22

needsSh : Sh a => a -> Int
needsSh x = shv x

top a = h a
  where
    h x = needsSh x

main = println (top True)
